Z||000012||theogre||02-10-2000||05:00 PM||||What he said...... <P>You have to reprogram the ECM.<P>You have to replace the MAP sensor.<P>You probably have to work on the TBI.<P>You really need the TBI to live on the intake side of the turbo which causes other problems. (Like you have to use a turbo with fuel proof seals. which are not installed in many turbos that are normally up stream from the fuel.) <P>If you put the TBI down stream from the turbo you have to compensate the fuel pressure regulator. You may also have to increase fuel pump pressure. You also have to figure out how to rework all the vacuum operated things connected to the TBI.<P>The Iron Duke is designed as an economy motor. It's not built for high HP applications. That I know of there was never e turbo version of it. Which means there is not even base programming for the ECM available. You would need someone to write an ECM setup from scratch.<P>It would be easier to take a 2.2l turbo motor and install that then upgrade the 2.5.<P>The V6 has it a bit easier. Some years of that motor and ECM were built to be shiped with a turbo. The correct MAP is even available for it. I am told even ECM control of the waste gate is posible if you add a few missing parts to the stock ECM.||||reg||1
