Z||000057||terryk||02-21-2000||11:08 PM||||I assume we are talking about a non-DIS engine right? You probably couldn't drive two TB injectors from the 6156(?). At the same time, I would consider an ECM swap to be part of the project.  There are a few out there that will work. The 7749 running the Sunbird code (with some changes) would run the two injectors with the injector driver jumpers swapped. <P>Frankly, I would fabricate a port intake and use the four injectors like the Sunbird and a V6 throttle body. If you look at the Sunbird, it's basically just 4 tubes into a larger tube with injectors pointing into the intake port. The longer the tubes, the better the low end.<P>If that makes your stomach goofy, then I might consider the 2.8L TB and 7747 ECM. That will drive it fine and supports HEI and SD. Just won't manage the boost, but that can be worked around (bypass valves).<P>As usual, supporting the blower is the bigger problem. Lot of weight bouncing around. Once the blower is mounted, fueling it is a smaller problem. <P>Regardless of what you do, you will need to make ECM calibration changes to make it run right.<P>On the adding of parts in the ECM, I don't believe that can be done on the 4 cyl HEI/SD ECM in the Fiero. Only the V6 Fiero's support boost, and the only circuit addition is the wastegate driver. It does support a knock sensor though (but not implemented in the Fiero V6).<P>This might be more work that it's worth.||||reg||1
Z||000058||FIEROCIOUS||02-22-2000||04:25 AM||||The turbo I plan to use on my Fiero is the T3 type it has a adjustable waste gate on it already, you just push or oull a rod on the side to vary boost pressure.<BR>We do not have a turbo for the 4 cyl (yet) we are still exploreing options but are leaning toward the T3 or a turbo off a 2.2 dodge. (they are plentiful around here)<BR>Kidzwheelz is hitting the phone tomarrow and is going to get what is needed for the computer. I do know you need a special MAP sensor and we have this in the works too.<BR>as for the vacume lines we devised a check valve (like on windseild squirters) this will make it so no positive pressure will act on esential vacume lines. We are looking at some thing to seal the throttle body from the atmostphere and have a few ideas from Holley. The stock exhaust manifold will probably be used for cost reasons, but will be re welded. This all banks pretty much on the computer problem but like I said Kidz is on the move! I probably forgot more than I remember but this is the just of what we have done.<P>SCCA: I'd be more than happy to talk to ya!<BR>You can talk to Kidzwheelz at PepBoys in Riverdale any given night after five. Or me and him on the weekends (I have anouther job) PepBoys is a hobby! LOL!<P>Kidzwheelz: AKA- PAT N PARTS<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000059||terryk||02-22-2000||01:31 PM||||What do you mean by "it takes a special map"?<BR>Do you mean map sensor? If the ECM isn't set up for a 2 bar map, it won't work. Gee, I wonder what the pre-7749 Sunbirds used for an ECM......<P>Maybe I'm missing something here.||||reg||1
