Z||000082||FIEROCIOUS||02-24-2000||06:11 AM||||Ok I have to get clareified here.<BR>The Ogre is talking about useing a dual injector to suply the extra fuel. <BR>From what? This seems too difficult. When you can......<P>Now you can increase fuel flow in two ways:<BR>1. injector pulse width.<BR>2. injector pressure.<P>There are limitations to both!<P>You can only run so much pulse width or duty cycle from a injector most injectors are stable to say 90% duty cycle. after that they become inconsistent. <P>Pressure can be risen at the expence of longevity, or util the pressure over comes the solinoid. <P>So we need more fuel!<BR>We can use a bigger injector at a lower duty cycle for normal operation, and simply increase the pulse width for boost.<P>What can we get a larger injector from?<P>Terry I know little about GMs computers and your going to have to walk me thru all of it!<BR>I do know that we need the dual map but I think it would be easiest to keep a ECM that has the same sensor inputs. We need only to change the prom to get this to work! I'm almost sure of this?<P>HotRod did hundreds of articles on tuboed dukes in the early 80s and they had ads for kits in the back!<BR>Can someone find some info on this?<P>We need a EASY cost effective computer not complete differant systems! <BR>Anyone have a prom burner?||||reg||1
Z||000083||Ozzy||02-24-2000||11:23 PM||||I'm not sure Fierocious but I think theogre was going down the path of another complete TBI unit that is already manufactured to house dual injectors rather than modifying the stock throttle body to house a larger injecter. This is assuming the physical dimensions are different than the stock injector on the 300 series. Then I have to ask about the 700 throttle body. I have the 88 Duck! If this is a reality I hope to do this to my car too. I think you guys are working on pre 87 engine specs??? Not to mention the DIS system and different ECM's??<P>Hey Phantom Rage...you seemed to have a truck load of parts and ideas. How are you fairing???<P>Ozzy<P>||||reg||1
